===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[appear]] as a featured performer or headliner, especially in an entertainment program.
#: {{ux|en|She '''starred''' in dozens of silent movies.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1902|author=Robert Marshall Grade|title=The Haunted Major
|passage=I was inundated with invitations; {{...}} I felt, indeed, much as a great actor must when he goes ''''starring'''' in the provinces.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[feature]] (a performer or a headliner), especially in a movie or an entertainment program.
#: {{ux|en|The show '''stars''' Calista Flockhart as a high-powered lawyer.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=David W. Menefee|title=The First Female Stars: Women of the Silent Era|page=4|passage="What followed this decision was exactly what we had expected: Mr. Fox, realizing that the public was tiring of Theda Bara in vampire roles, announced that he would '''star''' her in a production of Romeo and Juliet," she illustrated.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To mark with a star or [[asterisk]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To set or adorn with stars, or bright, radiating bodies; to [[bespangle]].
#* {{RQ:Young Night-Thoughts|314|Thy gloomy Grandeurs (''Nature''’s moſt auguſt, / Inſpiring Aſpect!) claim a grateful Verſe; / And, like a ſable Curtain '''ſtarr’d''' with Gold, / Drawn o’er my Labours paſt, ſhall cloſe the Scene.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[shine]] like a star.

